<title>FRANCE: Bouygues Offshore/Fluor Daniel JV in $75 mln deal.</title>
<headline>Bouygues Offshore/Fluor Daniel JV in $75 mln deal.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>French oil services firm Bouygues Offshore said on Wednesday its joint venture with Fluor Daniel BV signed a turnkey contract with the Bluewater group of the Netherlands for the supply of a floating production storage and off-loading unit.</p>
<p>Bouygues Offshore's wholly-owned subsidiary UiE Scotland Ltd will carry out the $75 million portion of the contract involving engineering, procurement, construction, installation and commissioning of the &quot;Bleo Holm&quot; hull, the French commpay said in a statement. Bouygues Offshore is a unit of construction firm Bouygues.</p>
</text>
